=begin
  libeo: the shared library for the e-scripts (ebounty, eloot, eherbs, ecleanse, eohunter, ...).

  Loaded once per session with Script.loadlib('libeo'); definitions persist after the
  library script exits. A script names the version it was built against and the library
  refuses a mismatch loudly:

    Script.loadlib('libeo')
    EO.require('0.3.0')

  This file only loads the library. The library itself is scripts/eo/, one file per
  concern, each readable on its own:

    eo/version.rb      EO.require / EO.version, the version gate
    eo/help.rb         EO.help, the help table every e-script prints
    eo/settings.rb     EO::Settings: whether the setup window can open, the settings table's
                       lookups and defaults, the ListSettingsForm helpers (the e-scripts')
    eo/travel.rb       EO.go2 / EO.at? / EO.nearest / EO.visit / EO.room_id
    eo/command.rb      EO.command / EO.result / EO.settle: send a command, wait out roundtime
    eo/containers.rb   EO::Containers: open a container only when it is closed, see one open,
                       read contents the game does not refresh (ebounty's and eloot's)
    eo/hands.rb        EO::Hands: free a hand, take, wear, put into a container, the READY list
                       (eloot's; outcomes come back as words for the driver)
    eo/town.rb         EO::Town: which shop to walk to and whether to go, a bounty town's region,
                       Four Winds Isle, the trash can, the locksmith pool's worker (eloot's)
    eo/items.rb        EO::Items: toss unless marked, phase and unphase a box, lift a curse,
                       the disk that follows you (eloot's)
    eo/locker.rb       EO::Locker: the character's locker rooms, getting into a booth, opening
                       it to a container, leaving (eloot's)
    eo/skinning.rb     EO::Skinning: who needs a blunt tool, getting ready, the skinning (eloot's)
    eo/appraisal.rb    EO::Appraisal: ask a shop what an item is worth, and read the answer (eloot's)
    eo/loot.rb         EO::Loot: what on the ground is loot, and which loot a policy wants (eloot's)
    eo/selling.rb      EO::Selling: sell one item and read the shop's answer (eloot's)
    eo/locksmith.rb    EO::Locksmith: the town locksmith (activator, open, fee) and the locksmith
                       pool (order, tips, the give, the list, depth, the return) (eloot's)
    eo/casting.rb      EO::Casting: the multicast count, casting at a target, making mana (wracking,
                       Sigil of Power, Symbol of Mana, stamina), another's active spells, bread (ewaggle's)
    eo/wander.rb       EO::Wander: a step anywhere (the Elemental Confluence too), picking a creature
                       to stop for, learning what TARGET accepts (ewander's)
    eo/hoard.rb        EO::Hoard: gem and reagent jars: label names, the kind check, reading a jar,
                       the stash inventory or a locker manifest, filling and shaking (eloot's)
    eo/cleanse/        EO::Cleanse: what the game does to a character, and the cure, from ecleanse
      tables.rb        the debuffs, hazards and TARGET answers; Policy; the spell for a job; can we cast
      hazards.rb       clouds, globes, webs and runestones: find, target, dispel, cleave, break
      afflictions.rb   poison, disease, magical debuffs, roots, stuns, webs; settling a room
      disarms.rb       the disarms not yet recovered (kept across restarts), searching, prying,
                       the floated weapon, the Sanctum's clench, a bonded weapon, the servant
      traps.rb         hive traps searched and disarmed, the itchy curse's safe room, the vat
    eo/coordination/   EO::Coordination: opt-in coordination between Lich sessions (eohunter's
                       strict group movement and safe-room hold). Loading starts nothing:
      protocol.rb      the read-only protocol, its server and client (bounded frames)
      discovery.rb     finding a peer session through Lich's active sessions
      operations.rb    explicitly granted operations, settled on the owner's tick
      parser_projection.rb  a read-only projection of Lich's parser state
    eo/guild/          EO::Guild: the Adventurer's Guild, from ebounty
      tables.rb        towns, NPC names and rooms, response texts, the task-type crosswalk
      policy.rb        TaskPolicy: which tasks a character takes, and why one is handed back
      npcs.rb          find an NPC, the taskmaster (Sailor's Grief sweep), a town's guards
      location.rb      a task's location to a start room and boundary list, capped
      forage.rb        herb rooms by tag and distance, herb name fixes
      taskmaster.rb    get, turn in, remove and expedite a task; boosts, vouchers, the cooldown
      assignments.rb   the furrier, herbalist and gem dealer visits that set a task
      guards.rb        the guard visit that sets or completes a task, heirloom in hand
      completion.rb    when a task is done enough to go to town; skin and gem counting
      heirloom.rb      the heirloom search: wander, SEARCH, stow; the helper spells
      escort_routes.rb the escort roads' special edges: climbs, sneaks, carts, the ferry
      escort.rb        the escort: the trip from the task, fetching the client, the road,
                       the room checks and the ambush watch (escortgo2's)
      disablers.rb     choosing and casting a disabling spell on the way (echild's)
      rescue.rb        the child: find it, its home, the walk to a guard (echild's), the
                       rescue script from ebounty with the garrote and Bard retries
    eo/herbs/          EO::Herbs: herbs and healing, from eherbs
      table.rb         every herb: where it is sold, what it cures, its doses; lookups
      injuries.rb      the next herb type a wound wants; can we cast; another's wounds
      doses.rb         the doses left in each item, learned from the game as it goes
      sack.rb          the herb sack: find, open, contents by form, store, take, the kit
      heal.rb          healing yourself from the sack, a dead player, an escort client
      shop.rb          the herbalist: menu, prices, buying, bundling, the shopping list

  What lives here is script-side glue that Lich itself should not carry. Anything that
  is a game rule or parser plumbing belongs in Lich itself (Stance, Stash.wield, Bank,
  Mana.pulse, issue_command, Spell state, the Bounty parser) and is called directly; a
  script that needs it raises its required Lich version.

        author: elanthia-online
  contributors: Nisugi
          game: Gemstone
          tags: library, utility, eo
      required: Lich >= 5.22.0
       version: 0.3.0

  Version Control:
  Major_change.feature_addition.bugfix
  v0.3.0 (2026-11-12)
    - EO::Settings: the setup window check, the settings table (get_category, get_setting,
      fill_defaults, prune) and the ListSettingsForm helpers, from the e-scripts' Setup
  v0.2.0 (2026-11-11)
    - split into scripts/eo/, one file per concern, shipped by the eohunter gem
    - EO.room_id, EO.command / EO.result / EO.settle, EO::Containers.open
    - EO::Guild: ebounty's task logic (tables, NPCs, the taskmaster finder,
      location resolution, herb lookup); the guild dialogue (get, turn in,
      remove, expedite, the assignment NPCs, the guards) with TaskPolicy
  v0.1.0 (2026-09-10)
    - initial: EO.require / EO.version, EO.go2 / EO.at? / EO.nearest / EO.visit,
      EO.help
=end

base = File.join(SCRIPT_DIR, 'eo')
verbose = $VERBOSE
begin
  $VERBOSE = nil
  %w[version help settings travel command containers hands town items locker skinning appraisal loot selling locksmith hoard casting wander
     cleanse/tables cleanse/hazards cleanse/afflictions cleanse/disarms cleanse/traps
     coordination/protocol coordination/discovery coordination/parser_projection
     guild/tables guild/policy guild/npcs guild/location guild/forage
     guild/taskmaster guild/assignments guild/guards guild/completion
     guild/heirloom guild/escort_routes guild/escort guild/disablers guild/rescue
     herbs/table herbs/injuries herbs/doses herbs/sack herbs/heal herbs/shop].each do |part|
    load File.join(base, "#{part}.rb")
  end
ensure
  $VERBOSE = verbose
end
